      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m reacquainting myself with this CL, so I apologize if I\u0027m retreading old ground or not understanding things I used to understand. I still think this looks pretty good.\n\nOverall areas of concern:\n1. I think you may have accidentally deleted some PE code that we still need for non-Servo boards during a rebase. If I\u0027m right, please fix that before submitting.\n2. I\u0027m still re-grokking the timer module changes, but I retain my earlier suspicion that the interface used on Servo could be closer to the non-Servo interface if not identical. If that\u0027s true, I\u0027d really like to avoid creating a second timer interface for Servo.\n3. There are a number of places where this CL does a config check for Servo before calling a function. Broadly, I think the code would be easier to follow if these config checks were for features (that Servo disabled in its board.h), and they were inside the relevant functions, not at each call site. Depending on the feature, some instances of this might be harder to change than others, and I\u0027d be OK with you submitting the CL with call site Servo config checks and then refactoring in a followup CL to have function definition feature config checks.",
      "revId": "233612fe45c5e63ea531e9bb8a114a3bdd1a4249",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
